# Keep the wall panel's USB hub and digitizer out of autosuspend.
#
# usbcore.autosuspend defaults to 2s and a kiosk touchscreen is idle almost
# always, so both devices are suspend candidates continuously. The panel's
# hub (1a40:0101) drops off the bus and does not re-present.
#
# See Machines.md#kitchen-hub, 2026-08-14.
#
# 2026-08-17: this did not fix it. Both devices have carried power/control=on
# since, and the hub still dropped twelve more times over the following three
# days, so autosuspend was not the cause. Two claims above are also wrong and
# are corrected here rather than deleted, because they shaped the design of
# the self-heal ladder:
#
#   - "nothing on the Pi can recover it" — rebinding xhci-hcd re-enumerates
#     the bus and brings both devices back in about a second, verified live.
#     kiosk-health.sh now has a usb_reset rung above reboot_touch.
#   - "only a full reboot drops VBUS" — true, and irrelevant: recovery never
#     needed VBUS to drop, only the controller to re-init.
#
# The rules stay. They cost nothing, autosuspend on a wall panel's digitizer
# is wrong regardless, and ruling a cause out is worth the two lines.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="1a40", ATTR{idProduct}=="0101", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="222a", ATTR{idProduct}=="0001", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
